      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T23:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I hadn\u0027t come across IDA.\n\nThe Pseudo IDs exist solely for userspace, they\u0027re not needed internally.\n\nI\u0027ve been thinking about removing Pseudo ID concept entirely...done now.  I carried it over from the original i2c-pseudo implementation, but I ended up never using it from iteflash.  The Pseudo IDs just aren\u0027t really that useful for solving the problem they were meant to help with.\n\n---\n\nThe situation they were meant to help with is determining when an I2C adapter number has been unexpectedly reused while a stateful i2c-dev client program is using a pseudo I2C bus - even if it\u0027s the same pseudo controller program that simply got restarted (e.g. crashed then restarted), and thus maybe using the same I2C adapter name.  If that happens the device program state may be out of sync.\n\nI no longer think this is of any real use.  It\u0027s still a race and there are other ways to make the same determination.",
      "parentUuid": "1fc3211a_363cd004",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 71
      },
