      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T23:46:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried to explain it with the comment - but clearly missed.\n\nThere is nothing different to do based on its return value.  This is to clear the completion in case `i2cp_cdev_ioctl_xfer_req()` was never called and therefore never consumed it.  That\u0027s why it\u0027s a \"try\" and why we don\u0027t care if it failed (that just means `i2cp_cdev_ioctl_xfer_req()` consumed it).\n\nSimilar situation for line 193.\n\nWhat\u0027s the right style in this case?  There\u0027s a compiler warning without the `(void)` of course.  Also the `(void)` makes it clear that ignoring the return value is deliberate.",
